For anyone who needs this on VSCode, this keybinding fixes it for Shift + Enter
```jsonc
//keybindings.json
[
    // ...
    {
        "key": "shift+enter",
        "command": "workbench.action.terminal.sendSequence",
        "args": {
            // "text": "\\\r\n"    // BAD: This breaks when attempting to add a new line mid sentence
            "text": "\u001b[13;2u" // GOOD: This seems to work much more nicely
        },
        "when": "terminalFocus"
    },
    // ...
]
```

**Updated:** 
This was updated to fix the bug because \\\r\n as the sequence only works when the caret is at the end. @yogan shared a better sequence adapted from @CSRessel's explanation below.

For those where this keybinding is a deal breaker, it can be solved with this comment's config:

https://github.com/sst/opencode/issues/1975#issuecomment-3192835872

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "keybinds": {
    "session_child_cycle": "none",
    "session_child_cycle_reverse": "none",
  },

  ...
}
```

